# HEAVY BAG POWER INTERVALS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Heavy Bag Power Intervals are high-intensity striking intervals performed against a heavy bag to maximize combat-specific power production, striking efficiency and anaerobic conditioning.

Within CAS, they are considered one of the highest-transfer conditioning exercises for striking-based combat sports.

---

# Philosophy

Strength developed in the weight room must eventually become combat performance.

Heavy Bag Power Intervals bridge this gap by teaching athletes to express maximal force through technically efficient strikes under realistic fatigue conditions.

CAS selects this exercise whenever the objective is to improve combat-specific power expression.

